</tr>
<tr>
<td>Snub roller</td>
<td>Increases belt wrap on the drive pulley so it can pull without slipping</td>
<td>Bearings, buildup on the roller face</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Take-up</td>
<td>Sets and holds belt tension as the belt stretches</td>
<td>Seized screws or slides, take-up travel used up by belt stretch</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Return rollers</td>
<td>Support the return side of the belt under the frame</td>
<td>Seized rollers that wear the belt, buildup on the roller shell</td>
</tr>
